# Brand Accent Color Rules

## Stack: Laravel + Inertia + Vue 3 — Light Theme with Client Accent Override

---

## Context

The project uses a **purchased light HTML/CSS/JS theme** as the base.
The client has provided two brand colors to use as **accent replacements only**.
The goal is to swap the theme's default pink/primary accent color with the client's Gold,
and use Navy for secondary accents, labels, and tags.

**Do not redesign the theme. Do not change backgrounds, typography, card layouts, or spacing.**
Only replace accent-colored elements.

---

## Client Brand Colors (Accent Use Only)

| Role             | Name | HEX       | When to use                                                                     |
| ---------------- | ---- | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Primary accent   | Gold | `#d9a800` | Replaces pink — buttons, CTAs, highlights, featured badges, active links, icons |
| Secondary accent | Navy | `#1a2a4a` | Labels, tags (For Sale, For Rent), section title underlines, hover overlays     |

---

## What to Replace

### ✅ Replace these with Gold `#d9a800`

- Primary buttons (the pink/red CTA buttons in the theme)
- "Featured" badges on property cards
- Active navigation link color
- Icon accent color (the outline icons that are currently pink)
- Hover underlines on links
- Progress bars or highlight strips
- "Add Listing" button background

### ✅ Replace these with Navy `#1a2a4a`

- Secondary tags like "For Sale", "For Rent" pill backgrounds
- Section label text (small uppercase labels above headings)
- Dark overlay badges on property card images
- Footer background (if dark variant is needed)
- Border accents on active/focused inputs

### ❌ Do NOT change

- White card backgrounds
- Light gray page backgrounds
- Body text color (dark gray / black from theme)
- Card layout, grid, spacing
- Typography (font family, sizes, weights)
- Any color that is not an accent/action element

---

## Tailwind Config Addition

Add only these two accent entries to your `tailwind.config.js`.
Do not replace the theme's full color palette:

```js
theme: {
  extend: {
    colors: {
      'brand-gold':  '#d9a800',
      'brand-navy':  '#1a2a4a',
      'brand-gold-hover': '#eecb3a',
      'brand-navy-hover': '#0a1526',
    },
  },
},
```

---

## CSS Override (app.css)

Add these variables and override classes after your theme's CSS import.
This avoids touching the theme source files directly:

```css
:root {
    --brand-gold: #d9a800;
    --brand-gold-hover: #eecb3a;
    --brand-navy: #1a2a4a;
    --brand-navy-hover: #0a1526;
}

/* Primary accent — replaces theme pink */
.btn-primary,
.badge-featured,
.nav-link.active,
a.accent {
    background-color: var(--brand-gold) !important;
    border-color: var(--brand-gold) !important;
    color: var(--brand-navy) !important;
}

.btn-primary:hover {
    background-color: var(--brand-gold-hover) !important;
    border-color: var(--brand-gold-hover) !important;
}

/* Secondary accent — replaces theme dark tags */
.badge-sale,
.badge-rent,
.tag-label {
    background-color: var(--brand-navy) !important;
    color: #ffffff !important;
}
```

