```

### For Sale / For Rent Tag (replaces dark theme tag)

```vue
<span class="bg-brand-navy text-white text-xs font-medium px-3 py-1 rounded">
  For Sale
</span>

<span class="bg-brand-navy text-white text-xs font-medium px-3 py-1 rounded">
  For Rent
</span>
```

### Active Nav Link

```vue
<a class="text-brand-gold border-b-2 border-brand-gold font-medium">
  Home
</a>
```

### Section Accent Underline

```vue
<h2 class="text-gray-900 text-2xl font-semibold">
  Discover Popular Properties
  <span class="block w-12 h-1 bg-brand-gold mt-2 rounded"></span>
</h2>
```

### Icon Accent Color

```vue
<!-- If theme uses inline SVG or icon fonts, override color only -->
<i class="theme-icon" style="color: var(--brand-gold)"></i>
```

---

## Hard Rules

1. **Only touch accent/action elements** — never touch backgrounds, body text, or layout classes from the theme.
2. **Gold replaces pink** — wherever the purchased theme uses its primary pink/red accent, use `#d9a800`.
3. **Navy replaces dark tags** — "For Sale", "For Rent", and similar labels use `#1a2a4a`.
4. **Never use Gold as body text on white** — contrast is too low. Gold is for backgrounds and icons only.
5. **Override theme CSS via `app.css`** — do not edit the purchased theme's source CSS files directly.
6. **Text on Gold background must be Navy** `#1a2a4a` — never white or black on gold.
7. **Text on Navy background must be white** `#ffffff`.

